A||||15||Lady Pegasus||I need help, please||||5||
Z||000000||Lady Pegasus||11-28-2001||09:31 PM||||One of my other posts got me thinking.  First of all, when does life get better?  Everyone always says after something tragic, life gets better.  B.S.  My father was taken from me too early in life. I was 15, he had just turned 41.  There are things that happened that made me feel like I was not a good enough kid while he needed me, and six years later,I'm still dealing with this pain.  My mother met someone else, and for years life was complicated with that situation (recovering alcoholic who would repeatedly slip up and vicious arguments would ensue).  Then, three years ago, my Grandmother passed from breast cancer right at the point in life where you really start appreciating the elders in the family.  I don't have any other grandparents now.  Then just this year, the baby of my  best friend (have known her my entire life) passed away.  He was a few weeks shy of his 2nd birthday.  He was a BEAUTIFUL baby boy.  Now my friend is using drugs and alcohol to cover things up.  Her husband is in the Air Force stationed in North Dakota.  She is in Illinois.  She has started seeing someone else, not telling her husband.  She tells her family that she is going out with me...but she's not.  This is putting me in an ackward position.  I know her husband well, and I love her.  I want to help her, but I know that she'll get upset if I  try talking to her. I don't know.  I'm just in a low point right now and I needed to vent.  Sorry.<P>------------------<BR>Hey pretty....don't you wanna take a ride with me...through my world?||||reg||5
Z||000001||California Kid||11-28-2001||09:40 PM||||She put you in the middle of a very serious condition.......no true friend would do that!!  You have to be honest with her, as well as the other loved ones in your life.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gary W||11-28-2001||09:58 PM||||Can only say that I've been there - Dad died when I was 18 (smoking-related heart disease). He was my inspiration for all things mechanical - got me into cars, etc. Just got over that loss when Mom was diagnosed with liver cancer when I was 20. She died when I was 21. The last of my grandparents died when I was 6. Never knew them. Had to grow up fast -dropped out of college, got a job and just did the best I could. I'm 35 now, and pretty comfortable with my life - I've done OK, I think they would be proud of me. The fond memories now outweigh the painful ones (Holidays are still tough) I'm not into the psycho-babble stuff, but I think you have to make your life into what you want. You can't always let circumstances and other people's lives drive your existence. I hope you can get past this, either on your own or with help from others. Don't be afraid to ask for help if you need it, or just vent. Looks like you've got some friends here.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Loki||11-28-2001||10:13 PM||||Well, im 25 and STILL waiting for life to "get better". Dont take that the wrong way, its different for everyone. Im going througha bad break up with my 10 month old son in the middle...I havnt seen him in 8 months (But im going to se ehim next month <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">) Just hang in there it all works out in time. Thats what ive been told and thats what I tell people. Im having to rely on like 3 friends up here and most of them dont do much with me anymore due to there "married".... Give it time, thats my only advise and so far has been good advise...<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/fieroloki/lokisig1%20copy.jpg">  <BR>"All Fieros broke right now" :(||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||11-28-2001||10:25 PM||||All that I can say is that time does tend to dull the pain somewhat. <BR>My mother died in 1972, when I was 15. Had some "elective" surgery. Needed blood. There was hepatitis in the blood they gave her. End of story.<BR>My father died in 1988, when I was 31. His mind was still very sharp, but his body just collapsed, over time. (He actually had been diagnosed with a form of muscular distrophy.) There were several times, after his passing, that I went to pick up the phone to give him a call. Ooops. Wrong.<BR>If anyting, I was thankful that neither of them suffered, though. <BR>It's always hard to lose a parent. Even more difficult when you are young. I was a bit jealous after my mom died, looking at all the kids who still had both parents. Just hang in there. You *will* be okay.  <BR>There is so much more I could say, but I don't want to ramble. <P>Oh... You should insist that your "friend" stops using you as cover when she's out running around. You don't need to allow her to make you a part of <I>that</I> situation. <BR>Just my $.02. <P>Best,<P>Raydar||||reg||1
Z||000005||MrPBody||11-28-2001||10:39 PM||||Losing a 2-year-old . . . I can't imagine it.  I don't <I>want</I> to imagine it!  Our daughter is 15 months, and is of course the sweetest and cutest baby in the world.  Losing her would be <I>awful</I>.  Babies die every day, but it's always someone else, somewhere else.  No wonder your friend is a basket case, particularly with her husband in North Dakota.  Do you think she would be open to the idea of counseling or a support group?<P>You probably can't keep covering for her, but it's tough to tell your best friend that she's screwing-up.<P>I don't think life "gets better"; I thing we get better at dealing with it.<P><BR><I>Edited for typos</I><P><p>[This message has been edited by MrPBody (edited 11-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||84fierotrevor||11-29-2001||06:07 AM||||damn.............................I wish my dad was dead! to bad it alway's happend's to the good dad's and never the bad one's.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Indy-2M4||11-29-2001||07:17 AM||||Lady...It sounds like you have enough to deal with the past things in your life and your "friend" (we shall say loosly), shouldn't be USING you as a skapegoat. You really need to talk to her, and if she gets mad, then she is showing here true colors and not the friend she claims to be. No friend should USE another.  Girl, get on with your life and start with talking to her. To start the healing proccess, you will have to confront these issues. I wish you the very best of luck, and I'll pray for you.<P>Kathy||||reg||1
Z||000008||falconhulk||11-29-2001||08:41 AM||||Life definitely gets better.  But then it gets bad again.  then better, then bad......<BR>Life is constant up and downs on diffrent levels.  Even while the entire nation has been having a rough time my life has been much better in the last couple months.  You just have to look for the positives.  Keep working towards a goal.  Things really do work out.  Sometimes they just take longer then WE think they should.  I think they call this realization ......FAITH.  Thats what gets you through the hard times.  Thats what tells you in the back of your head that its going to be better.  Focus on how you want life to be and DO WHAT YOU HAVE TO DO to make it like that.  Only people that will never appreciate the things they have are given anything for free.  The rest of us have to work hard or lie down and give up.<BR>Your job is not the only thing you have to work hard at.  The harder you work at life the better it is.  Mostly your life does not get better but your preception of life does.  This is becasue you no longer feel powerless.  Hang in there and work hard.  Its worth it.||||reg||1
Z||000009||JSocha||11-29-2001||09:26 AM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.twinoaks4fun.com/smilies/sad06.gif"> <P>Hey me Lady! <P>I don't know what to say to cheer you up a tad as I'm deeply saddened to hear about the events in your life.  I sincerely hope things do turn around and get better for yah.  Your PFF family is always here for you as well.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||84Bill||11-29-2001||10:15 AM||||Aww that bites. Just be a good friend to her as I'm sure you are and above all that keep your faith. Life is a PITA but we all gotta do it, I don't know why, maybe someday I/We will. Until then keep plugging away with the daily dregs, breathing these petulant vapors and hoping for a better day that always seems just a whisper out of reach.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||artherd||11-30-2001||01:10 AM||||I don't know what to say, what do you tell a mother who just watched her *CHILD* die?   How do you tell her to knock off using you, shape up and quit fooling around?<P>I don't know how to do that.<P>Live is what you make of it though, that's what makes us human.<P>Best!<BR>Ben<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000012||avengador1||12-01-2001||08:13 PM||||As the saying say's: Time heals all wounds. Im sorry to hear about all your loses. I too miss my departed grandparents. Only my father's mother is left.I don't know how I will feel when she too is gone, I don't even want to think about when my parents pass. All I can say is we all pass on someday and maybe we will be reunited in the great beyond. Meanwhile I am sure that they would want you to continue on with your life and that they are there with you in spirit. I can still feel my grandfather's presence sometimes. As for your "friend" what she is doing to her husband is not right and he WILL find out about it eventually. She has made her bed and will have to sleep in it. My best friend cheated on his wife and told me about it before he did. I told him not to do it because he would stand to loose it all. He finally had to tell his wife about the affair because the other woman was going to spill the beans on him, because he would not see her again. His wife ended up not being able to forgive him and now they are divorced. She just remarried but still cannot forgive him. You seem like an intelligent, young, beautifull woman with your whole life ahead of you. There sure will be great times ahead (marriage,children,etc.) but there could also be more bad times ahead. You have to take what life gives you and try to do the best you can. Take life one day at a time and enjoy what you can. Don't dwell on bad times. Hope this helps.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||Ken Wittlief||12-01-2001||09:02 PM||||when we are kids we think life is like a fairy tale and we will all live happily everafter.<P> Real life isnt like that - we all have to face and deal with death and loss and suffering and pain. Some of us deal with it better than others, some of us come out stronger in the end and see these things as a test of our character - others see them as an excuse to do whatever we darn well feel like doing.<P> The most important thing is whether you have to go through these things alone - or if you have friends who will carry you when you cant stand on your own anymore.<P> If sounds like your friend has lost it compeletely  - maybe she is blaming herself for her sons death and is subconciencely sabotaging her own life now.<P> She needs help - she needs consuling at least. As for yourself the best advice i can give is to surround yourself with the best people you can find, and dont be afraid to lean on them when you feel like life is too hard to bear.<P> You cant pick your family or the circumstances you were born into, but you can make the best of what you have now, and go from there.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Lady Pegasus||12-02-2001||03:04 PM||||Thanks you guys.  I really do appreciate everything you've said.  I was having a really bad day, you know how it is.  One thing just seems to pile on the other.  I haven't talked to myfriend in a week, just haven't called her.  So we shall see where life will take us from here.  Thank you once again.<P>------------------<BR>Hey pretty....don't you wanna take a ride with me...through my world?||||reg||6
